  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt -1pt; text-indent: 36pt; text-align: justify;">General and administrative expense was $5.7 million, or 25% of total revenue, for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2026, compared with $5.6 million, or 25% of total revenue, for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2025, representing an increase of approximately 2%. The increase was primarily attributable to higher personnel-related costs, including stock-based compensation and employee benefit costs, as well as increased liability insurance premiums, bad debt expense and travel-related costs.</p>
  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt -1pt; text-indent: 36pt;">&#160;</p>
